{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then encode the exploration policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy favors random_walk in clear/search conditions, inserts a short move_forward pulse after a clear exploratory pulse to bias coverage, and uses one-shot turn-recovery states for obstacle events. Uncontrollable events are total in every specification state, with path_clear usually self-looping in action/commit states so intended pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and motion into simple plants and place the exploration logic in specifications",
    "Use exactly one controllable action per explore/recovery state, with random_walk in the initial clear state, short forward progress after clear exploration, and directed turns for left/right/front obstacles"
  ],
